=== a native that pops its operands and then raises ===
PASS: the value under the entry stack is untouched
PASS: the sequence is restored
PASS: the index is restored
PASS: the error sits on top
=== a compound body that fails partway ===
PASS: the value under the entry stack is untouched
PASS: the consumed input is restored and the partial values are gone
PASS: the body's error sits on top
=== a body that consumes below its own inputs ===
PASS: every consumed value comes back
=== the handler idiom drops the body's inputs with the error ===
PASS: only the value below survives
PASS: the handler answers none
PASS: parse?(rfc3986) leaves nothing behind on a reject
PASS: parse?(rfc3986) rejects ! in the scheme
=== a body that does not raise ===
PASS: the body's own stack stands
=== nested recovers ===
PASS: the outer entry stack is restored and the inner leftovers are gone
PASS: the outer handler sees its own error
PASS: a recover in a handler starts from the handler's stack
PASS: the inner handler ran
=== try with a curried input ===
PASS: an in-range read is ok
PASS: a failed try leaves only its result
PASS: an out-of-range read is an err
PASS: try takes a quotation that always raises
